<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of South</p>
<p>American Libertadores Cup, first round soccer matches played</p>
<p>Wednesday.</p>
<p>Group one</p>
<p>In Asuncion: Cerro Porteno (Paraguay) 0 Guarani (Paraguay)</p>
<p>1 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorer: Toribio Caballero (19)</p>
<p>In Sucre, Bolivia: Oriente Petrolero (Bolivia) 0 Bolivar</p>
<p>(Bolivia) 4 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers: Antonio Vidal Gonzalez (31), Miguel Mercado (48</p>
<p>and 51), Carlos Borja (58)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Bolivar		1  1  0  0  4  0  3</p>
<p> Guarani		1  1  0  0  1  0  3</p>
<p> Cerro Porteno	1  0  0  1  0  1  0</p>
<p>Oriente Petrolero  1  0  0  1  0  4  0</p>
<p>Next match: February 25 - Oriente Petrolero v Cerro</p>
<p>Porteno</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p>In Guayaquil, Ecuador: Emelec (Ecuador) 2 Nacional</p>
<p>(Ecuador) 1 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Emelec - Luis Escobar (28), Graciani (85)</p>
<p>Nacional - Kleber Chala (75)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>In Buenos Aires: Racing Club (Argentina) 1 Velez Sarsfield</p>
<p>(Argentina) 2 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Racing Club - Fernando Queiroz (63)</p>
<p>Velez Sarsfield - Patricio Camps (38 and 49)</p>
<p>Standings</p>
<p> Emelec		1  1  0  0  2  1  3</p>
<p> Velez Sarsfield   1  1  0  0  2  1  3</p>
<p> Nacional	    1  0  0  1  1  2  0</p>
<p> Racing Club	 1  0  0  1  1  2  0</p>
<p>Next match: February 26 - Nacional v Velez Sarsfield</p>
<p>Group three</p>
<p>In Puerto Ordaz, Venezuela: Mineros (Venezuela) 0 Minerven</p>
<p>(Venezuela) 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,000</p>
<p>In Santiago: Universidad Catolica (Chile) 2 Colo Colo</p>
<p>(Chile) 2 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Universidad Catolica - Luis Perez (29), Javier Margas (62)</p>
<p>Colo Colo - Fernando Vergara (10 and 79),</p>
<p>Standings</p>
<p> Colo Colo			 1  0  1  0  2  2  1</p>
<p> Universidad Catolica	  1  0  1  0  2  2  1</p>
<p> Minerven			  1  0  1  0  0  0  1</p>
<p> Mineros			   1  0  1  0  0  0  1</p>
<p>Next match: February 25 - Universidad Catolica v Mineros</p>
<p>Group four</p>
<p>In Belo Horizonte, Brazil: Cruzeiro (Brazil) 1 Gremio</p>
<p>(Brazil) 2 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Cruzeiro - Ailton (24)</p>
<p>Gremio - Ze Alcino (10), Emerson (63)</p>
<p>Attendance: 33,000</p>
<p>In Lima: Sporting Cristal (Peru) 0 Alianza (Peru) 0</p>
<p>Standings</p>
<p> Gremio			    1  1  0  0  2  1  3</p>
<p> Alianza			   1  0  1  0  0  0  1</p>
<p> Sporting Cristal		1  0  1  0  0  0  1</p>
<p> Cruzeiro			  1  0  0  1  1  2  0</p>
<p>Next match: February 25 - Alianza v Cruzeiro</p>
<p>Note: top three teams in each group qualify for the second</p>
<p>round. Holders River Plate (Argentina) have a bye to the</p>
<p>second round.</p>
